  "track": "track-07",
  "title": "Browser DOM events storage observers and navigation APIs",
  "status": "source-backed-draft-generation-enabled",
  "concepts": [
    "The DOM is a standards-defined object model for document trees, events, and abortable operations.",
    "The browser exposes HTML markup through typed interfaces such as Document, Node, and Element rather than as plain strings.",
    "DOM changes have synchronous tree semantics while rendering, layout, and paint are separate browser work.",
    "Events travel through capture, target, and bubble phases and can be canceled independently from propagation.",
    "Observers report selected asynchronous changes without polling and should be disconnected when their work ends."
  ],
